          "description": "Define a control volume at the sodium metal or sodium-ion electrode and solid electrolyte interface. Adapt material-and-energy-balance formalism from flow chemistry to write conservation equations for Na atoms/ions, electronic charge, heat, and side-product mass [Author et al., 2019](https://openalex.org/W3011563721). The balance residual is the local mismatch between incoming Na+ flux, Na+ transported through the electrolyte, Na consumed by side reactions, and electronic leakage. Use a coupled characterization-simulation workflow to parameterize the model with ionic conductivity, electronic conductivity, exchange current density, chemical potential, elastic modulus, and interphase thickness [Author et al., 2021](https://openalex.org/W4200315733). The model outputs a target anion-ratio profile for a sulfide-chloride solid electrolyte, using the tunable anion ratio as the design handle [Author et al., 2025](https://openalex.org/W4410507001)."
