          "description": "Fabricate a dense thin interlayer, for example 5 to 20 micrometers, in which the Cl/(S+Cl) or related anion ratio changes monotonically from the sodium-facing side to the bulk-electrolyte-facing side. The gradient is the structured intervention intended to distribute Na+ flux and block local electronic leakage. Use dry pressing, tape casting, or sequential vapor deposition under dry-room conditions to create the gradient. Produce controls with the same average composition, total thickness, density, and surface roughness but with a uniform composition, a randomized multilayer sequence, an anti-gradient profile, and single-composition layers representing the gradient endpoints. The use of sulfide-chloride solid electrolytes with tunable anion ratios provides the chemical space for these controlled variants [Author et al., 2025](https://openalex.org/W4410507001)."
