          "description": "Build a phase-field model of the Na|sulfide-chloride interface that couples Na+ concentration, electric potential, local Cl/S anion ratio, electronic carrier density, side-reaction extent, and chemomechanical strain, following the phase-field coupling of thermodynamics, kinetics, and electrochemistry used for battery electrodes [Author et al., 2024](https://openalex.org/W4398203391). The model will define a dimensionless flux-balance number, F, as the ratio of local Na deposition/side-reaction demand to local Na+ transport plus chemical/mechanical relaxation capacity. Rate-limiting-step analysis will identify whether ionic transport, electronic leakage, interphase reaction, or strain accumulation dominates failure [Author et al., 2022](https://openalex.org/W4205252019). The calibrated model will output a critical threshold F_c and spatial maps showing where interfacial designs fail."
